      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BELLABAMA (6) is long overdue and won't get a better chance to break through. Has placed 6/9 so far, four of them on wet ground and extra trip a plus now she's at her top. Hard to beat. STEAL AWAY (8) is yet to break through in seven runs but is another close to a win. Finished fourth after being prominent at the turn at her last appearance over 1600m at Bairnsdale on August 4. Both career minors have been in heavy ground. Main danger. Race drops away outside that pair. GOOD LORDY ME (3) returned from a spell two-and-a-half weeks ago when he was in the firing line on the corner before being beaten 6 lengths into seventh over 1400m at Sale. Likely improver with top-three prospects. GREY SABRE (4) is fitter for two runs back and can improve sharply. CHURCHILL LANE (2) was disappointing last time but gets his chance to atone.",
